The sister's name has 4 more letters than half of the letters in Indras' name.
So, $n_S = \frac{1}{2} \times n_I + 4 = \frac{1}{2} \times 6 + 4 = 3 + 4 = 7$.
The total number of letters in Indras' and her sister's names is $n_I + n_S = 6 + 7 = 13$.

